  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Social  Protection Policy Support Programme, Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Social Protection Policy Support (SPPS) Programme is a flagship programme of the Cabinet Division and General Economics Division of Bangladesh Planning Commission for social security reforms in Bangladesh. The Programme acts as a catalyst for enrolling the National Social Security Strategy (NSSS) and its guided reforms, by ensuring the broadest stakeholder participation, expert advice, and capacity development. The project proposal addresses reform gaps: National Social Security Strategy (NSSS) action plans and their short and medium-term implementation. The Programme commenced in 2014 and is being implemented with the support of the Government of Bangladesh (GoB), DFAT, FCDO (formerly known as DFID), and UNDP.</narrative>
  </description>
